<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:33:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany sticks to Russia sanctions after Trump diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40082699e963fca54bd4f796bec91f20781360e99099c611508a3ee6cdd05550</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:33:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sticks-to-russia-sanctions-after-trump-diesel-deal/live-79627811--7157e47a4e48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sticks-to-russia-sanctions-after-trump-diesel-deal/live-79627811?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Washington announced a sanctions pause on Russian diesel, Germany has said it remains committed to pressuring Moscow and supporting Ukraine. More on DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Two German officials shot dead during routine gun inspection in Bavaria; suspect arrested after overnight standoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ba891221a2f3b16e4b1d8792773d524976aa288c4ec07524ad71256326a8655</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T05:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/two-german-officials-shot-dead-during-routine-gun-inspection-in-bavaria-suspect-arrested-after-overn/live-79607225--1b63007f86d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/two-german-officials-shot-dead-during-routine-gun-inspection-in-bavaria-suspect-arrested-after-overnight-standoff/live-79607225?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A routine inspection of legally owned firearms turned deadly in Bavaria. Police spent hours negotiating with an armed suspect before storming his home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224f082c59f6fe29f2c649ce513f9dada024dbce3912240b212e6fcb1bca78ac</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:33:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Operations Plan Germany: How the Bundeswehr trains for NATO collective defense</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de945962c543a63fa1118a6a6bdec06240188dabae581191c62f78bc763e9abe</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:33:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T12:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/operations-plan-germany-how-the-bundeswehr-trains-for-nato-collective-defense/a-79553793--d1447370a9ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/operations-plan-germany-how-the-bundeswehr-trains-for-nato-collective-defense/a-79553793?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">How prepared is Germany for national defense? The answer lies in the Operations Plan Germany. Military exercises such as "Red Storm Charlie" are designed to put these preparations to the test in realistic scenarios.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Macron and Steinmeier struggle to revive Franco-German ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55e51a29f4f93dda9eff1cc9d4389982c3c793c8429f3d50b32d61f085f3931a</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/macron-and-steinmeier-struggle-to-revive-franco-german-ties/a-79618635--64b747b714b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/macron-and-steinmeier-struggle-to-revive-franco-german-ties/a-79618635?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Presidents Frank-Walter Steinmeier and Emmanuel Macron are about to step down from their offices. Their meeting in France made it clear how urgently the Franco-German partnership needs new momentum.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany women's football team: Can Ena Mahmutovic make a case to become Germany's next No.1 goalkeeper?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2af13874c120c14bf51f094fcf388cdc277a86dffa8124211fe47a4c27784240</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-women-s-football-team-can-ena-mahmutovic-make-a-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeepe/a-79609341--5da82027e599.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-women-s-football-team-can-ena-mahmutovic-make-a-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The women's friendlies against Australia and Japan present an opportunity for Ena Mahmutovic to make her case for succeeding Ann-Katrin Berger as Germany's first-choice goalkeeper.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ex-German Chancellor Schröder attends Putin's birthday bash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9aa49672af03e293bbab964ef405f3b4dba0c4803d355f8290ba2cd3572fac47</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T22:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ex-german-chancellor-schr_der-attends-putin-s-birthday-bash/a-79606017--884ded06e661.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ex-german-chancellor-schröder-attends-putin-s-birthday-bash/a-79606017?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Chancellor Gerhard Schröder still maintains a friendship with Russian leader Vladimir Putin. Tensions are high between Germany and Russia as the invasion of Ukraine continues.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-10-10T14:32:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
